titre$Exidia  Peter Roberts 2016 
com$ adapt GF 11/2016
1,0$ source : British fungi - Keys  http://www.fieldmycology.net/
1,0$

1,2$ Fruitbodies hyaline to whitish, occasionally tinted pink to violaceous
1,3$ Fruitbodies distinctly coloured, orange, brown or black

2,0$ #1) Mature fruitbodies whitish; effused, becoming plicate; no mineral inclusions; basidia not stalked $ thuretiana (Lév.) Fr
2,0,n$Descriptions, Lists & Icons:///D+I: in Breitenbach, J., Kränzlin, F., Fungi of Switzerland Non gilled fungi, Heterobasidiomycetes, Aphyllophorales, Gasteromycetes 2: 412 pp. (1986), p. 64, pl. 24///D: in Hansen, L. & Knudsen, H., Nordic Macromycetes Heterobasidioid, Aphyllophoroid and Gasteromycetoid Basidiomycetes 3: 444 pp. (1997), p. 100

 <http://www.fieldmycology.net/gbchklst/gbsyns.asp?intGBNum=1675>

2,0$ Mature fruitbodies hyaline to whitish, occasionally tinted pink to violaceous; pustular and coalescing; white mineral inclusions often visible; basidia distinctly stalked $ nucleata  (Schwein.) Burt
2,0,n$Descriptions, Lists & Icons:///D: in Hansen, L. & Knudsen, H., Nordic Macromycetes Heterobasidioid, Aphyllophoroid and Gasteromycetoid Basidiomycetes 3: 444 pp. (1997), as Myxarium nucleatum, p. 109

 <http://www.fieldmycology.net/gbchklst/gbsyns.asp?intGBNum=1833>
3,4$ #1) Fruitbodies blackish-brown to black; hymenium with scattered warts or papillae under lens
3,5$ Fruitbodies orange to brown; hymenium smooth

4,0$ #3) Fruitbodies turbinate, often remaining separate, occasionally coalescing; typically on oak or hazel $ glandulosa  (Bull.) Fr.
4,0,n$Descriptions, Lists & Icons:///D+I: in Phillips, R., Mushrooms and other fungi of Great Britain & Europe: 288 pp. (1981), p. 263///D+I: in Breitenbach, J., Kränzlin, F., Fungi of Switzerland Non gilled fungi, Heterobasidiomycetes, Aphyllophorales, Gasteromycetes 2: 412 pp. (1986), p. 62, pl. 21///D: in Hansen, L. & Knudsen, H., Nordic Macromycetes Heterobasidioid, Aphyllophoroid and Gasteromycetoid Basidiomycetes 3: 444 pp. (1997), p. 100


<http://www.fieldmycology.net/gbchklst/gbsyns.asp?intGBNum=1832>    
4,0$ Fruitbodies effused, irregularly lobed, coalescing; typically on beech, willow, sycamore and other deciduous trees #but rarely, if ever, on oak) $ plana Donk

<http://www.fieldmycology.net/gbchklst/gbsyns.asp?intGBNum=39201>

5,0$ Fruitbodies brown, irregularly lobed; on pine $ saccharina (Alb. & Schwein.) Fr.
5,0,n$ Descriptions, Lists & Icons:///D: in Hansen, L. & Knudsen, H., Nordic Macromycetes Heterobasidioid, Aphyllophoroid and Gasteromycetoid Basidiomycetes 3: 444 pp. (1997), p. 101
<http://www.fieldmycology.net/gbchklst/gbsyns.asp?intGBNum=6336>    
5,6$ Fruitbodies ornage to orange-brown; on deciduous trees
6,0$ Fruitbodies button-shaped; typically on birch $ repanda Fr.
6,0,n$Descriptions, Lists & Icons:///D: in Hansen, L. & Knudsen, H., Nordic Macromycetes Heterobasidioid, Aphyllophoroid and Gasteromycetoid Basidiomycetes 3: 444 pp. (1997), p. 101
 <http://www.fieldmycology.net/gbchklst/gbsyns.asp?intGBNum=9747>   

6,0$ Fruitbodies turbinate, often pedulous; typically on willow $ recisa (Ditmar) Fr.
